00:40:21,820 --> 00:40:31,460
我用过执行计划，那是我们发布的一个早期版本，有点像一种原型技能，
说明你应该如何用里程碑和验收标准来构建计划。
I've used exec plans, which was kind of like an early version of this that we published,
which is sort of like a proto-skill that says this is how you should structure a plan with milestones and acceptance criteria.

369
00:40:33,038 --> 00:40:35,600
我还没在护栏工程中真正使用过规划模式。
I haven't really used plan mode as part of the harness at all.

370
00:40:35,800 --> 00:40:45,440
我这里的预期是，我应该能直接丢进去一个工单，让它去完成任务，而不需要经过规划环节，
因为大多数时候我根本不会去读它。
My sort of expectation here is that I should be able to drop a ticket in and have it do the job anyway without diverting through a
plan, because most of the time I'm never going to read it anyway.

371
00:40:46,180 --> 00:40:54,820
所以我发现，如果你确实使用计划，并且在完全不阅读的情况下批准它，
你实际上是在编码一系列你未必真的想遵循的指令。
So I find that if you do use a plan and you approve it without reading it at all,
you're actually encoding a bunch of instructions that you don't necessarily all you want followed.

372
00:40:55,440 --> 00:41:09,444
所以如果你打算使用计划，我的建议是把这些计划作为独立的 PR 推送，只包含计划内容，
让真人去审查每一行，并在合并和启动之前获得人工批准。
So if you are going to use plans, my recommendation is to push those up as single PRs with just the plan,
where you actually have humans review every line of it and block on human approval before they get merged and then kicked off.

373
00:41:10,510 --> 00:41:17,180
因为你实际上可能会在包含糟糕指令的部署过程中浪费时间。
Because you're effectively potentially wasting your time on a rollout with instructions that are bad.

374
00:41:17,646 --> 00:41:20,080
所以你要尽量减少这种情况发生的时间。
So you want to minimize the time that happens.

375
00:41:20,206 --> 00:41:30,920
但我确实认为，让 Token 在 CI 中消耗是这里必要的一部分，因为写代码不再是难点。
But I do think that kind of getting tokens to be spent in CI is a necessary part here,
because writing code no longer is the hard part.

376
00:41:31,100 --> 00:41:38,260
就像，让代码被接受并推动代码和产品前进，这才是让写出来的代码产生价值的关键。
Like, getting code accepted and advancing the code and product forward is, like, what it takes to make that written code be valuable.

377
00:41:39,060 --> 00:41:43,960
而且你知道，大家都听过那句格言，比如，资深工程师会提供高质量的代码审查。
And you know, kind of have all heard the aphorism that, like, you know, senior engineers give good code reviews.

378
00:41:44,040 --> 00:41:46,680
就像，我们也期望作为 Agent 的资深工程师能做到同样的事情。
Like, we expect our senior engineers as agents to do the same.

379
00:41:47,182 --> 00:41:52,200
有人问，代码是可丢弃的构建产物吗？
Someone asked, is code a disposable build artifact?

380
00:41:53,500 --> 00:41:53,740
是的。
Yes.

381
00:41:54,820 --> 00:42:00,780
我想我们通过 Symfony 触及了这一点，那是我们发布的一个 Agent 编排器。
I think we touch on this with Symfony, which is sort of this agent orchestrator that we released.

382
00:42:00,880 --> 00:42:10,820
这个想法是，你知道，我们可以发布一个库，它实际上
是一个定义非常明确的规范，而代码是它的编译产物。
This idea that, you know, we can publish a library that's actually a super well-defined spec that the code is a compiled artifact of.

383
00:42:11,182 --> 00:42:18,840
而且我认为把 LLM 当作模糊编译器是一个很有意思的心智模型，对吧？
And I think like using LLM as fuzzy compiler is like an interesting mental model to have, right?

384
00:42:18,900 --> 00:42:31,160
就像我们在护栏工程的代码库中放入的所有上下文，实际上就像是约束和优化传递，
用来判断哪些代码最初是可以被构建的。
Like all of the context that we're putting in the code base for harness engineering is effectively like constraints and optimization
passes on which code is acceptable to build in the first place.

385
00:42:31,566 --> 00:42:40,260
这与类似 LLVM 在编译 Rust 代码过程中进行的静态分析和优化传递非常相似。
And this is pretty similar to like the static analysis and optimization passes
that something like LLVM would do in the process of compiling Rust code.

386
00:42:41,120 --> 00:42:52,340
而把一个模型换成另一个模型，有点像把 Rust 编译器的代码生成后端从 LLVM 换成 Cranelift。
And sort of swapping out one model for another is sort of like changing your
code generation backend from, you know, LLVM to Cranelift in the Rust compiler.

387
00:42:52,782 --> 00:43:06,596
你会期望所有关于什么是可接受的 Rust 代码的规则，都能在后端产生有效的、可靠的机器码，
即使生成过程不同，并且你最终得到不同的 x86 指令。
And you would expect that all of the sort of rules around what acceptable Rust code looks like produce valid sound machine code at the
back, even if the generation process is different and you end up with different x86 instructions.

388
00:43:07,182 --> 00:43:11,380
所以对于 LLM 也是同样的思维，就是更换不同的模型之类的。
So same sort of mindset for LLMs, of swapping out different models sort of thing.

389
00:43:11,694 --> 00:43:20,740
我们希望围绕代码的结构基本上能限制它的编写方式，使其符合我们的要求。
We want the structure around the code to basically limit how it is written to things that would be acceptable to us.

390
00:43:21,838 --> 00:43:26,200
从高层次来看，你能给我们描绘一下你正在构建的未来吗？
At a high level, can you give us a picture of what future you're building for?

391
00:43:26,542 --> 00:43:27,700
上下文仍然重要吗？
Does context still matter?

392
00:43:28,110 --> 00:43:31,680
人们如何进行工程，护栏工程，上下文工程？
How do people do engineering, harness engineering, context engineering?

393
00:43:32,046 --> 00:43:33,120
未来看起来是什么样的？
What does the future look like?

394
00:43:35,790 --> 00:43:48,760
我想要构建的未来是这样的：我可以拿出一个 Token 预算，然后把一个季度、
半年甚至一年的工作量放入其中。
Sort of the future that I want to build toward here is where I'm able
to take a token budget and a quarter, a half, or a year's worth of work.

395
00:43:50,126 --> 00:43:52,180
拿人类的输入来排序。
take the human input to rank.

396
00:43:52,238 --> 00:44:05,700
确定哪些是最重要的，包括成功指标、可靠性指标，然后交给机器，
让它们持续工作并推动我的产品前进，而不需要我亲自动手操作。
what is most important, success, metrics, reliability metrics, give it to the machines,
and have them continually work and advance my product forward without my hands explicitly on the wheels at all.

397
00:44:05,742 --> 00:44:21,920
随着我们从非常早期的原型设计走到内部 Alpha、内部 Beta、外部 Alpha，
我感觉软件工程流程中的新环节基本上都是从零开始的。
As we have gone through very early prototyping to internal alpha, internal beta, external alpha,
I kind of have felt that new parts of the software engineering process have kind of started from zero.

398
00:44:22,100 --> 00:44:31,980
我们必须建立起能力，就像这些五角形的性格图表一
样，我在某些方向上很强，但在某些地方可能比较弱。
and we've had to build up capability, kind of like these pentagonal
personality charts, where I spike in this direction, maybe I'm weak over here.

399
00:44:31,980 --> 00:44:44,080
而且，你知道，当我们第一次部署软件时，Agent 在产品发
布前对我们构建的产物进行 QA 冒烟测试的能力是很弱的。
And, you know, when we get to deployed software for the first time, right, the agent's ability to do, like,
QA smoke testing on our built artifacts before they're promoted to distribution was weak.

400
00:44:44,180 --> 00:44:45,620
我们之前没在这方面投入任何时间。
We hadn't invested any time in this.

401
00:44:45,680 --> 00:44:46,280
没有任何文档。
There were no docs.

402
00:44:46,380 --> 00:44:56,300
没有任何工具让 Agent 可以用来下载构建好的产物、启动它、到处检查，
以确保我们最关键的用户旅程得到了充分的验证和测试。
There were no tools that the agents could use to, like, download the built artifact, launch it, poke around to make sure that our,
like, most critical user journeys were well validated and tested.

403
00:44:56,300 --> 00:45:04,740
所以，因为我不想亲自去碰电脑，我们需要找出让 Agent 自己构建工具来完成那部分工作的办法。
So, because I don't want to be touching the computer, we needed to figure out, like,
ways for the agents to build themselves tools to do that part.

404
00:45:06,860 --> 00:45:11,160
除了写代码之外，软件工程还有一整个宇宙的内容，对吧？
And there's a whole universe of software engineering outside of writing code, right?

405
00:45:11,220 --> 00:45:14,340
比如，我在对用户反馈进行故障排查，我在对页面进行故障排查。
Like, I am triaging user feedback, I'm triaging pages.

406
00:45:14,958 --> 00:45:20,380
我在确保生产环境的日志中没有泄露任何 PII。
I am making sure that we don't have any PII leaking in the logs in production.

407
00:45:20,878 --> 00:45:23,460
我在确保 Twitter 上的舆论氛围是良好的。
I'm making sure that, like, the Twitter vibes are good.

408
00:45:23,460 --> 00:45:36,860
我在确保人们喜欢我的软件，确保我们的用户运营人员拥有编写良好的运行手册支持，
让他们能够排查并缓解大量的用户问题，然后再把这些内容转化到代码本身中。
and people are enjoying my software, that our user operations staff are supported with well-written run books that allow them to
triage and mitigate high-volume user issues, and then moving that into the code itself.

409
00:45:36,860 --> 00:45:38,140
这样问题从一开始就不会发生。
so they don't happen in the first place.

410
00:45:38,680 --> 00:45:52,630
既然我不再需要产出代码，我的思维就可以转向这些其他更高层次或更模糊的活动，
但 Agent 也足够出色到能做这些事，而弄清楚如何写下流程和验收标准，
And as I no longer have to produce code, like, my mind can shift to these other higher-level or more squishy activities,
but the agents are good enough to do these things, too, and figuring out how to write down the processes and the acceptance criteria

411
00:45:52,630 --> 00:45:52,650
就变成了利用这些 Agent 来完成工作的元编程部分。
And as I no longer have to produce code, like, my mind can shift to these other higher-level or more squishy activities,
but the agents are good enough to do these things, too, and figuring out how to write down the processes and the acceptance criteria

412
00:45:52,650 --> 00:45:57,220
就变成了利用这些 Agent 来完成工作的元编程部分。
becomes like the sort of like metaprogramming part of the job using these agents.

413
00:45:57,742 --> 00:45:58,920
这是个很棒的结尾。
That's a great way to end it.

414
00:45:58,980 --> 00:45:59,820
真是个令人兴奋的功能。
What an exciting feature.

415
00:46:00,206 --> 00:46:01,100
大家给 Ryan 掌个手。
Give it up for Ryan, guys.

416
00:46:01,240 --> 00:46:01,820
谢谢大家。
Thank you, folks.

417
00:46:01,820 --> 00:46:01,860
谢谢。
